2026-07-01","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Crime and Disorder Joint Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-05","committee":"Human Resources Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-06","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Resources Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-23","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-09","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-21","committee":"Resources Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Resources Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"New","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.basingstoke.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Building Control cost-recovery monitoring process not started as of early September, with October completion target one month away","lead":"Auditor recommendation for formal cost-recovery monitoring suggests questions about whether the service currently self-finances or requires general-fund subsidy. A finance director needs visibility of which services run at cost and which are subsidized.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Standby generator installation at Wade Road deferred from 2026 to 2027-28, postponing critical business continuity infrastructure","lead":"Deferral of flagged-priority business continuity infrastructure indicates capital constraints or shifting risk priorities. The facility operates without adequate backup power until 2028.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Waste and Recycling Services contract indexation position unresolved in September, disputed invoices to be reviewed once rates are settled","lead":"Unresolved contractual disputes represent financial uncertainty and potential liability for disputed invoicing. The scope and direction of any billing adjustment remain unknown.","iso":"2026-09-28","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","headline":"Building Control cost-recovery monitoring process not started as of early September, with October completion target one month away","detail":"Auditors recommended formalizing a three-year rolling cost-recovery review to determine whether Building Control aligns fee levels to the full-cost-recovery principle. As of early September, work had not been started; the responsible officer is only 'proposing' to engage Finance to complete it. Target completion is October 2026.","category":"income","matters":"Auditor recommendation for formal cost-recovery monitoring suggests questions about whether the service currently self-finances or requires general-fund subsidy. A finance director needs visibility of which services run at cost and which are subsidized.","figures":"No current figures provided; three-year rolling monitoring framework to be established","quote":"Liaison to occur with BDBC Finance to introduce a documented three-year rolling cost recovery review to monitor cumulative surpluses or deficits and ensure fee levels remain aligned to the full-cost recovery principle","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","headline":"Standby generator installation at Wade Road deferred from 2026 to 2027-28, postponing critical business continuity infrastructure","detail":"Installation of a standby generator at Wade Road, marked Significant risk, has been deferred to next financial year (2027-28) pending planning permission and IT coordination. Initially flagged as requiring 'upmost priority', installation is now postponed by approximately one year.","category":"capital","matters":"Deferral of flagged-priority business continuity infrastructure indicates capital constraints or shifting risk priorities. The facility operates without adequate backup power until 2028.","figures":"No cost disclosed","quote":"The installation of a stand-by generator, integrated with the UPS at Wade Road should be given the upmost priority","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 2 Remaining Recs","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004624/500004624.pdf","headline":"Waste and Recycling Services contract indexation position unresolved in September, disputed invoices to be reviewed once rates are settled","detail":"An unresolved commercial dispute exists over contract indexation and billing rates with the council's waste contractor. Variable invoices and credit notes require review and adjustment once the indexation position is resolved, including restatement of default amounts previously billed. As of early September the matter remained 'Ongoing. Subject to negotiation' with a December 2026 target, marked COMMERCIAL IN CONFIDENCE.","category":"income","matters":"Unresolved contractual disputes represent financial uncertainty and potential liability for disputed invoicing. The scope and direction of any billing adjustment remain unknown.","figures":"Supporting values marked COMMERCIAL IN CONFIDENCE; documented as 'values excluding and including indexation'","quote":"Once the indexation position has been resolved, variable credit notes/invoices issued should be reviewed in detail to ensure they reflect correct contract rates","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","paper_title":"Report","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004618/500004618.pdf","headline":"Treasury portfolio outperforming peer benchmarks on returns with lower credit risk","detail":"In benchmarking against 226 council participants, Basingstoke's treasury portfolio achieved weighted average return of 4.15% against benchmark average of 3.93%, while holding significantly lower credit risk (1.00 vs 1.76). The council has also lengthened investment maturities to 289 days average vs 52 days for peers, locking in fixed rates and providing income certainty.","category":"other","matters":"Demonstrates effective treasury management generating superior returns while managing risk prudently, indicating capable finance leadership.","figures":"Return 4.15% vs benchmark 3.93%; credit risk indicator 1.00 vs benchmark 1.76; maturity 289 days vs 52 days","quote":"The average return being achieved by the council is above the benchmark average. The average maturity indicates that the council has fixed many of its interest rates for a longer period than the benchmark average and this provides the council with a greater certainty of its future investment income. The council also holds investments with much lower credit risk than the average.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-28","committee":"Audit and Accounts Committee","paper_title":"Report","paper_url":"https://basingstoke.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s500004618/500004618.pdf","headline":"Council approves expanded lending to future merger partners Rushmoor and Hart ahead of April 2028 reorganisation","detail":"On 16 July 2026, the council approved amendments to the Treasury Management Strategy allowing loans to Rushmoor Borough Council and Hart District Council to exceed the standard \u00a310M individual counterparty limit. These councils are expected to merge with Basingstoke and Deane on 1 April 2028 as part of the proposed Local Government Reorganisation.","category":"governance","matters":"Signals structural change to the council's operating model with major governance transition planned for April 2028, creating potential risks and opportunities for merged entity's financial management.","figures":"Individual counterparty limit raised beyond \u00a310M for Rushmoor and Hart; merger date 1 April 2028","quote":"It is expected that these councils will merge with Basingstoke and Deane Borough Council on 1st April 2028 as part of the proposed Local Government Reorganisation.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-16"},"name":"Basingstoke & Deane","findings_total":88,"news_drafts_total":3}}